{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016DFWa89SXdXias1avEsFFV","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\"\"\"attavo: the command.\n2\t\n3\t    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\n4\t    attavo spec-gate [N]\n5\t    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\n6\t    attavo approval-status [N]\n7\t    attavo build [N]\n8\t    attavo verify [N]\n9\t    attavo file-findings [N]\n10\t    attavo file-stops [N]\n11\t    attavo counsel [N]\n12\t    attavo record-only\n13\t    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\n14\t    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready] [--again] [--report]\n15\t    attavo drive --all\n16\t    attavo worker N <build|verify> NN\n17\t    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n18\t    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n19\t    attavo test [N] [--all | <test>...] [--fresh]\n20\t\n21\tThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts five proofs against a\n22\ttenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n23\t\n24\t  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n25\t                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\n26\t                             and carries a non-empty retires\n27\t  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\n28\t                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\n29\t                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\n30\t                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\n31\t  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\n32\t                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\n33\t                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\n34\t                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\n35\t                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\n36\t                             carries its own record paths this way)\n37\t  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n38\t                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\n39\t                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n40\t                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n41\t                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n42\t                             heading when a build failed after running\n43\t                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\n44\t                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n45\t                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n46\t                             never refused\n47\t  5. every-attested-item-is-sealed\n48\t                             every merged item that carries a record for\n49\t                             every stage has a statement in the forge's\n50\t                             attestation store for its merge commit, read\n51\t                             through [forge].attestation_command -- a\n52\t                             merge at or before [forge].sealed_since is\n53\t                             named as before the window instead of failed.\n54\t                             [forge].attestation_command exiting 2 means\n55\t                             the store itself could not be read, reported\n56\t                             as not_read by item and never as unsealed\n57\t  6. no-attested-item-is-empty\n58\t                             no attested item is empty: every merged,\n59\t                             fully-staged item's passing build record\n60\t                             names a change, sha not equal to start_sha.\n61\t                             [doctor].built_since names a commit at or\n62\t                             before which merges are named as before the\n63\t                             window instead of failed, so the specimen\n64\t                             that motivated this proof stands on the\n65\t                             record without failing the tenant forever;\n66\t                             absent, the window is proof three's. A build\n67\t                             record with no start_sha is counted as not\n68\t                             readable, never as failed.\n69\t\n70\tNothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\n71\tblocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\n72\tis done.\n73\t\n74\tspec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\n75\tfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\n76\tis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\n77\tbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\n78\trejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\n79\teven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\n80\tbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\n81\tfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\n82\tthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\n83\tone enforces.\n84\t\n85\tbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\n86\tdeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\n87\tapproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\n88\t(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\n89\tGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\n90\tconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\n91\tspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\n92\tbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\n93\tevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\n94\tdeclared \"reports\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\n95\tit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\n96\tnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\n97\tsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\n98\ttests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\n99\twhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\n100\twhole-tree check, all three run in a detached worktree of HEAD and\n101\tnever in the executor's own directory: the gate reads the commit, not\n102\tthe tree, so a path written and never committed cannot pass a\n103\tcriterion, a test, or a check on the executor's behalf. An iteration\n104\tthat ends with HEAD unchanged since start_sha is told, in the feed and\n105\tthe log, that the executor committed nothing and that the gate reads\n106\tthe commit, and iterates; the last iteration ending that way halts the\n107\tbuild instead of failing it, stop class empty, provenance executor,\n108\tdetail naming that the executor committed nothing and how many paths\n109\tit left modified or untracked. pass requires every criterion,\n110\tthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0, and HEAD\n111\tto have moved since start_sha; any non-zero exit iterates, with the\n112\tfailure as feedback, up to a fixed budget. [checks] is optional; a\n113\ttenant that declares none is not refused. Before the adapter is invoked\n114\tit asks whether this machine can\n115\trun the checks -- of [checks].probe, run once inside [checks].probe_timeout_s\n116\t(exit 0 yes; anything else, or the bound, an environment refusal), or,\n117\tfor a tenant that declares no probe, by running [checks].command whole\n118\t(exit 2 no) -- and says both the question and the answer in the feed\n119\t(issue #212). The adapter is given ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND, `attavo test N`,\n120\tand ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S when [tests].call_timeout_s is declared; it\n121\tis not given the tenant's checks. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\n122\tthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\n123\texits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\n124\tunder an \"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\n125\tit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n126\t{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\n127\talready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\n128\tbuild contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the full rules it\n129\tenforces.\n130\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a752ff7-c430-4cfd-9b9a-21883129b5e6","uuid":"2be4d28c-586e-4b7b-a650-247a3d5484c5","timestamp":"2026-09-27T20:33:02.585Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-237/attavo/cli.py","content":"\"\"\"attavo: the command.\n\n    attavo doctor [TENANT_ROOT] [--json]\n    attavo spec-gate [N]\n    attavo approve [N] --by LOGIN\n    attavo approval-status [N]\n    attavo build [N]\n    attavo verify [N]\n    attavo file-findings [N]\n    attavo file-stops [N]\n    attavo counsel [N]\n    attavo record-only\n    attavo attest [--partial] [N]\n    attavo drive [N] [--until-ready] [--again] [--report]\n    attavo drive --all\n    attavo worker N <build|verify> NN\n    attavo ledger [N] [--json]\n    attavo stops [N] [--json]\n    attavo test [N] [--all | <test>...] [--fresh]\n\nThe doctor is the definition of done. It asserts five proofs against a\ntenant root and exits 1 until every proof holds:\n\n  1. every-gate-rejects      every gate in the manifest's [gates] table,\n                             run against its rejection fixture, exits non-zero,\n                             and carries a non-empty retires\n  2. one-item-every-stage    one work item under paths.records carries a\n                             record for every stage -- spec, approval,\n                             build, verify -- all four introduced by one\n                             merge commit reachable from HEAD\n  3. no-commit-lacks-record  every commit on the default branch after the\n                             manifest was introduced is named by a record's\n                             sha or commits list, or itself writes under\n                             paths.records (a record is committed with the\n                             code it describes; an item's merge commit\n                             carries its own record paths this way)\n  4. no-stop-lacks-cause     every build or verify record under\n                             paths.records at record_version 3 or later,\n                             with a status other than pass, carries a stop\n                             naming an enumerated class and provenance, a\n                             non-empty detail when unclassed, the gates\n                             heading when a build failed after running\n                             them, and the tool's own error line when an\n                             adapter exit ended the log -- records before\n                             record_version 3 are counted and reported,\n                             never refused\n  5. every-attested-item-is-sealed\n                             every merged item that carries a record for\n                             every stage has a statement in the forge's\n                             attestation store for its merge commit, read\n                             through [forge].attestation_command -- a\n                             merge at or before [forge].sealed_since is\n                             named as before the window instead of failed.\n                             [forge].attestation_command exiting 2 means\n                             the store itself could not be read, reported\n                             as not_read by item and never as unsealed\n  6. no-attested-item-is-empty\n                             no attested item is empty: every merged,\n                             fully-staged item's passing build record\n                             names a change, sha not equal to start_sha.\n                             [doctor].built_since names a commit at or\n                             before which merges are named as before the\n                             window instead of failed, so the specimen\n                             that motivated this proof stands on the\n                             record without failing the tenant forever;\n                             absent, the window is proof three's. A build\n                             record with no start_sha is counted as not\n                             readable, never as failed.\n\nNothing in doctor is a gate. The doctor reads; it never writes and it never\nblocks a merge by itself. It is what CI runs to say whether the product\nis done.\n\nspec-gate, approve, and approval-status are gates and writers. They run\nfrom the tenant root (the current working directory); N, the work item id,\nis read from the ATTAVO_ITEM environment variable when set, else from the\nbranch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\nrejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\neven while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\nbranch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\nfile under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\nthe spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\none enforces.\n\nbuild refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\ndeclares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\napproval-status would print valid. It exports the executor's identity\n(issue #33) into the adapter's environment as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\nGIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL, set by the product and never the tenant's git\nconfig, then invokes the named adapter (adapters/<name>/run) with the\nspec, the corpus, and the branch. It refuses (status refused) a commit\nbetween start_sha and HEAD not authored by that identity, checks that\nevery path touched matches a spec claim, records the adapter's own\ndeclared \"reports\" -- the fields adapters/<name>/conformance.json says\nit can supply with a real value (issue #41), so a field it claims and\nnever supplies is a defect the conformance suite catches rather than a\nsilent null -- then runs the criteria, the\ntests [tests].select and [tests].run name for the touched paths, and --\nwhen the manifest declares [checks].command -- the tenant's own\nwhole-tree check, all three run in a detached worktree of HEAD and\nnever in the executor's own directory: the gate reads the commit, not\nthe tree, so a path written and never committed cannot pass a\ncriterion, a test, or a check on the executor's behalf. An iteration\nthat ends with HEAD unchanged since start_sha is told, in the feed and\nthe log, that the executor committed nothing and that the gate reads\nthe commit, and iterates; the last iteration ending that way halts the\nbuild instead of failing it, stop class empty, provenance executor,\ndetail naming that the executor committed nothing and how many paths\nit left modified or untracked. pass requires every criterion,\nthe test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0, and HEAD\nto have moved since start_sha; any non-zero exit iterates, with the\nfailure as feedback, up to a fixed budget. [checks] is optional; a\ntenant that declares none is not refused. Before the adapter is invoked\nit asks whether this machine can\nrun the checks -- of [checks].probe, run once inside [checks].probe_timeout_s\n(exit 0 yes; anything else, or the bound, an environment refusal), or,\nfor a tenant that declares no probe, by running [checks].command whole\n(exit 2 no) -- and says both the question and the answer in the feed\n(issue #212). The adapter is given ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND, `attavo test N`,\nand ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S when [tests].call_timeout_s is declared; it\nis not given the tenant's checks. It writes the next build-NN.json under paths.records/N/, with\nthe adapter's transcript -- each iteration's gate output (criteria\nexits, the selected tests' stdout, the tenant's checks' tail) appended\nunder an \"--- attavo gates, iteration N ---\" heading, issue #89 -- beside\nit as build-NN.log. Every record whose status is not pass carries stop:\n{class, provenance, detail}, derived from the refusal, halted, and log\nalready on hand (issue #89); a pass record carries stop: null. See the\nbuild contract in the project's Phase 2 issue for the full rules it\nenforces.\n","numLines":130,"startLine":1,"totalLines":417}}}
