{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0187V6h9aec7LkMFqnHetDRX","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\nindex 70a96ac..a7780b7 100644\n--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml\n@@ -51,13 +51,7 @@ jobs:\n       - name: pytest\n         if: steps.inherit.outputs.inherit != 'true'\n         run: >\n-          python3 -m pytest tests -q --durations=5\n-          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects\n-          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage\n-          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record\n-          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause\n-          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_attested_item_is_sealed\n-          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_attested_item_is_empty\n+          python3 -m pytest tests -q --durations=5 -m 'not own_records'\n       - name: pytest end\n         if: steps.inherit.outputs.inherit != 'true'\n         run: echo \"PYTEST_END=$(date +%s)\" >> \"$GITHUB_ENV\"\n@@ -139,8 +133,8 @@ jobs:\n         with:\n           python-version: \"3.11\"\n       - run: pip install pytest jsonschema\n-      - name: doctor's five proofs\n-        run: python3 -m pytest tests/test_doctor.py -q -k \"every_gate_rejects or one_item_traversed_every_stage or no_commit_lacks_a_record or no_stop_lacks_cause or every_attested_item_is_sealed\"\n+      - name: the tests that read this repository's own records, the doctor's proofs among them\n+        run: python3 -m pytest tests -q -m own_records\n       - run: python3 bin/attavo doctor .\n \n   action-self-check:\ndiff --git a/attavo.toml b/attavo.toml\nindex 47c5df5..231e157 100644\n--- a/attavo.toml\n+++ b/attavo.toml\n@@ -37,7 +37,7 @@ retires = [\n [tests]\n select = \"python3 .attavo/bin/select-tests\"\n call_timeout_s = 240\n-run = \"xargs -r python3 -m pytest -q --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_attested_item_is_sealed --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_attested_item_is_empty\"\n+run = \"xargs -r python3 -m pytest -q -m 'not own_records'\"\n \n [paths]\n specs = \"attest/specs\"\ndiff --git a/attavo/cli.py b/attavo/cli.py\nindex 3d27b84..4b467dd 100644\n--- a/attavo/cli.py\n+++ b/attavo/cli.py\n@@ -78,9 +78,13 @@ branch (attavo/N-*). The doctor's first proof sets ATTAVO_ITEM for a\n rejection fixture's own item, so a gate's own command needs no argument\n even while the enclosing repository sits on a real item's attavo/N-*\n branch. Every run of spec-gate or approve writes the next numbered attempt\n-file under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. See\n-the spec contract in the project's Phase 1 issue for the full rules each\n-one enforces.\n+file under paths.records/N/ and never overwrites one already written. A\n+fix item's spec names the root-cause bucket its change closes as one line\n+in the problem, \"Bucket: <slug>\"; spec-gate refuses a bucket the tenant's\n+buckets.md (beside paths.specs) does not list, or any bucket when that\n+file does not exist, before any criterion runs -- a spec with no bucket\n+line is not asked for one. See the spec contract in the project's Phase 1\n+issue for the full rules each one enforces.\n \n build refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest\n declares [executor].build and [tests].select and [tests].run, and unless\n@@ -154,7 +158,11 @@ selected, the exit code, and the seconds spent (or that the answer came\n from the cache). It is the one test command an executor is given (issue\n #212); the product's own transport -- drive, worker, build, verify,\n counsel, file-stops -- refuses to run at all when ATTAVO_STAGE is set,\n-since the transport is the pass's, not the executor's.\n+since the transport is the pass's, not the executor's. The tests that\n+read this repository's own records carry @pytest.mark.own_records, the\n+only vocabulary that tells them apart from the rest of the suite;\n+[tests].run and CI's full-suite step exclude them (-m 'not own_records')\n+and the doctor job and CI's inherit path run only them (-m own_records).\n \n verify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has\n status pass, and unless the manifest declares [forge].checks_command --\ndiff --git a/attavo/spec.py b/attavo/spec.py\nindex 8cf623c..e263ca5 100644\n--- a/attavo/spec.py\n+++ b/attavo/spec.py\n@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@\n from __future__ import annotations\n \n import os\n+import re\n import shutil\n import subprocess\n import sys\n@@ -22,6 +23,10 @@ from attavo.records import latest_record, write_record\n \n # --- the spec contract ---\n \n+BUCKET_LINE = re.compile(r\"^Bucket:\\s*([a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*)\\s*$\")\n+BUCKET_ENTRY = re.compile(r\"^- ([a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]*):\\s+\\S\")\n+\n+\n def parse_spec(spec_md: Path) -> tuple[dict[str, Any] | None, str | None]:\n     lines = spec_md.read_text().splitlines()\n     heading_idx = [i for i, l in enumerate(lines) if l.startswith(\"## \")]\n@@ -36,6 +41,15 @@ def parse_spec(spec_md: Path) -> tuple[dict[str, Any] | None, str | None]:\n     idx_problem, idx_claims, idx_criteria = heading_idx\n     claims = [l.strip()[2:].strip() for l in lines[idx_claims + 1:idx_criteria]\n               if l.strip().startswith(\"- \")]\n+    # A fix item names the root-cause bucket its change closes, as one\n+    # line in the problem: \"Bucket: <slug>\". Optional; when present the\n+    # gate checks it against the tenant's closed list (bucket_refusal).\n+    bucket = None\n+    for l in lines[idx_problem + 1:idx_claims]:\n+        m = BUCKET_LINE.match(l)\n+        if m:\n+            bucket = m.group(1)\n+            break\n     criteria = []\n     for l in lines[idx_criteria + 1:]:\n         s = l.strip()\n@@ -43,7 +57,35 @@ def parse_spec(spec_md: Path) -> tuple[dict[str, Any] | None, str | None]:\n             continue\n         name = s[2:].split(\":\", 1)[0].strip()\n         criteria.append(name)\n-    return {\"claims\": claims, \"criteria\": criteria}, None\n+    return {\"claims\": claims, \"criteria\": criteria, \"bucket\": bucket}, None\n+\n+\n+def buckets_path(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any]) -> Path:\n+    \"\"\"The tenant's closed list of root-cause buckets: buckets.md beside\n+    the specs directory (attest/buckets.md when specs live in attest/specs).\n+    One bucket per line, \"- <slug>: <one sentence>\".\"\"\"\n+    return root / Path(m[\"paths\"][\"specs\"]).parent / \"buckets.md\"\n+\n+\n+def listed_buckets(path: Path) -> list[str]:\n+    if not path.is_file():\n+        return []\n+    return [mm.group(1) for mm in (BUCKET_ENTRY.match(l) for l in path.read_text().splitlines()) if mm]\n+\n+\n+def bucket_refusal(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any], bucket: str | None) -> str | None:\n+    \"\"\"A spec that names a bucket must name one the tenant lists. Symptom\n+    counts do not converge; bucket counts can, and only if every bucket a\n+    fix item names is one the list already carries or an item added on\n+    purpose. No bucket line, no check: a capability item has no bucket.\"\"\"\n+    if bucket is None:\n+        return None\n+    path = buckets_path(root, m)\n+    if not path.is_file():\n+        return f\"bucket: {bucket} named but {path.relative_to(root)} does not exist\"\n+    if bucket not in listed_buckets(path):\n+        return f\"bucket: {bucket} is not listed in {path.relative_to(root)}\"\n+    return None\n \n \n def run_criterion(exe: Path, cwd: Path) -> int:\n@@ -194,6 +236,9 @@ def cmd_spec_gate(argv: list[str]) -> int:\n     results: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n     if refusal is None:\n         # parse_spec returns a refusal exactly when it returns no spec.\n+        parsed 